1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,816
Narrator: Scenario 89. Changes, security, and disaster recovery.

2
00:00:07,416 --> 00:00:19,032
B: What evidence will demonstrate a successful disaster recovery exercise? I want criteria that cover business service, not just servers starting in the recovery region.

3
00:00:19,632 --> 00:00:31,320
A: The approved objectives are a sixty-minute recovery time objective and a five-minute recovery point objective. We'll measure both using the documented exercise boundaries.

4
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:43,656
C: Please explain when that recovery clock starts and stops. Business teams may define recovery differently if customers can log in but cannot finish transactions.

5
00:00:44,256 --> 00:00:54,864
A: For this exercise, timing starts at the simulated disaster declaration and stops when the agreed business checks pass, including order submission and payment confirmation.

6
00:00:55,464 --> 00:01:06,312
B: How will we verify the recovery point? A healthy replication indicator alone may miss transactions that were acknowledged but never reached the recovery site.

7
00:01:06,912 --> 00:01:19,344
A: We'll compare transaction identifiers and durable timestamps with the source record captured at declaration. Any gap must be reconciled and evaluated against the five-minute objective.

8
00:01:19,944 --> 00:01:34,008
C: My team will validate representative orders and check downstream accounting. Who will verify identity access, network routing, external integrations, and monitoring in the recovery region?

9
00:01:34,608 --> 00:01:46,680
A: Each dependency has a named owner in the exercise checklist. We'll confirm their availability before starting and record limitations where the test uses simulated integrations.

10
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:59,784
B: We also need a safe return plan. Switching back before data synchronization is verified could create inconsistent records or lose transactions written during recovery operations.

11
00:02:00,384 --> 00:02:13,728
A: Agreed. Failback requires separate checks, reconciliation, and authorization. We'll keep the recovered service active until the return conditions in the runbook are satisfied.

12
00:02:14,328 --> 00:02:26,448
C: Please send the checklist by November 18 at 14:00 UTC. I'll confirm the business validators and the exact transactions they need to inspect.

13
00:02:27,048 --> 00:02:39,744
B: We'll review readiness at that checkpoint. After the exercise, report actual recovery time, measured data gaps, business results, and any limits on what was demonstrated.
